# Findings the image scan in .github/workflows/cd.yml may skip. Trivy reads
# this file from the checkout root. Every entry says why, and the expiring
# entry fails the scan again after its date, so it cannot be forgotten.

# next 14.2.35: RCE on Windows-hosted servers only (GHSA-p293-qw3h-jr36). The
# image runs on Linux (node:24-alpine), so the vulnerable path does not exist.
CVE-2026-75604

# next 14.2.35: RCE through sharp/libheif when the Image Optimization API
# optimizes an AVIF file. Trivy flags it by package version, so it keeps
# reporting it until Next itself is upgraded (15.5.24+ or 16.3.3+, ticket 15),
# but the vulnerable path is closed: next.config.mjs sets images.unoptimized,
# so /_next/image answers 404 and nothing reaches the optimizer (ticket 13,
# pinned by src/__tests__/next-config-images.test.ts). The expiry stays so the
# upgrade cannot be forgotten: after it the scan fails again until ticket 15
# lands.
GHSA-2xp9-vwfh-vxw4 exp:2026-10-10
